WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.014
A Flask or FastAPI app
marks user-facing strings,

2
00:00:05.014 --> 00:00:06.756
picks each request's locale,

3
00:00:06.756 --> 00:00:08.961
and loads that
locale's translations.

4
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:11.751
Flask apps usually use Flask-Babel,

5
00:00:11.751 --> 00:00:14.943
which picks the locale and
loads gettext catalogs.

6
00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:20.027
General Translation's CLI fills
those catalogs for every language

7
00:00:20.027 --> 00:00:20.607
you ship.

8
00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:26.700
Point a pot entry in gt.config.json
at the English PO catalog.

9
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:31.864
Run npx gt translate,
then pybabel compile,

10
00:00:31.864 --> 00:00:34.196
and the app loads the
compiled catalogs.

11
00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:41.303
The experimental gt-flask and
gt-fastapi SDKs translate inline

12
00:00:41.303 --> 00:00:43.275
t strings without catalogs.

13
00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:46.273
Your team now ships
Spanish with each release.
